(4870431, 706747, 83313, '<td valign="top">Lots of posterization in the sky, which is really hard to avoid in a shot like this. <br/> <br/>Your file size of only 64k indicates a highly compressed image and that is robbing a lot of the detail from this image. I can see a lot of blocky compression artifacts in the grass and around the edges of the trees. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)<br/> <br/>It is a good scene, but the previously mentioned technicals hurt it, I''m afraid.</td>', 'Lots of posterization in the sky, which is really hard to avoid in a shot like this.  Your file size of only 64k indicates a highly compressed image and that is robbing a lot of the detail from this image. I can see a lot of blocky compression artifacts in the grass and around the edges of the trees. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one) It is a good scene, but the previously mentioned technicals hurt it, I''m afraid.', '2008-08-06 14:35:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(4870433, 707228, 83313, '<td valign="top">Awwwww!!! Great poster material here!</td>', 'Awwwww!!! Great poster material here!', '2008-08-06 14:36:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(4870444, 707450, 83313, '<td valign="top">Looks familiar...<br/> <br/>No vote from me on this since I know whose it is. I can still see some grainy noise in the sky on this using the calibrated monitor at work. It''s noticeable, but not really bad. I''m curious if others will mention it. If this were advanced editing you could have cleaned that noise up without hurting the rest of the image.</td>', 'Looks familiar... No vote from me on this since I know whose it is. I can still see some grainy noise in the sky on this using the calibrated monitor at work. It''s noticeable, but not really bad. I''m curious if others will mention it. If this were advanced editing you could have cleaned that noise up without hurting the rest of the image.', '2008-08-06 14:41:31.000000', NULL, 1),
