(5031945, 706734, 42013, '<td valign="top">Fantastic picture... leading lines, a road, cool clouds. Makes me want to wander.</td>', 'Fantastic picture... leading lines, a road, cool clouds. Makes me want to wander.', '2008-10-29 21:07:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5080731, 706981, 67841, '<td valign="top">It''s a beautiful ride on a bike up through the UP.  I''m originally from the northwest side (up in the Keweenaw) and did a 2 week photography/camping expedition across the UP on my old ''80 Suzuki GS850 a couple of summers back and it was a blast.  I did stop in Munising, but only grabbed a couple of shots of Miner''s Castle.  This shot of yours shows how much I really need to take one of those sunset cruises there (I still go up at least twice a year).<br/> <br/>Congrats on a great image &amp; a top ten finish!</td>', 'It''s a beautiful ride on a bike up through the UP.  I''m originally from the northwest side (up in the Keweenaw) and did a 2 week photography/camping expedition across the UP on my old ''80 Suzuki GS850 a couple of summers back and it was a blast.  I did stop in Munising, but only grabbed a couple of shots of Miner''s Castle.  This shot of yours shows how much I really need to take one of those sunset cruises there (I still go up at least twice a year). Congrats on a great image & a top ten finish!', '2008-11-23 22:38:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5161989, 706734, 67258, '<td valign="top">This is lovely - the tonal range is really good and the curve and leading line superb.  I haven''t ever visited the Peak District; I shall have to put that to rights in 2009.</td>', 'This is lovely - the tonal range is really good and the curve and leading line superb.  I haven''t ever visited the Peak District; I shall have to put that to rights in 2009.', '2009-01-01 06:29:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(5198143, 707470, 30222, '<td valign="top">cute how the radical crop works sublime in this entry</td>', 'cute how the radical crop works sublime in this entry', '2009-01-17 09:25:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5240158, 706981, 57775, '<td valign="top">Wow, I love this - very serene and beautiful.  Makes me want to go there to see it for myself.</td>', 'Wow, I love this - very serene and beautiful.  Makes me want to go there to see it for myself.', '2009-02-05 00:23:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5244567, 707315, 16230, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GUTomek:</b></div><hr/><i> I love Mt. Hood and you framed it beautifully.  From Timothy Lake?  I really like the light, the reflection and the clarity of all your details from close to far.  Would be very interested in knowing what you did to make this pop.  Congratulations! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes, I believe it''s Timothy Lake, I found it through GPS on my route to Mt. Hood. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>This is definitely Trillium Lake, near the boat ramp. It''s not possible to get a view of Mt. Hood like this from Timothy Lake.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by william88: Originally posted by GUTomek: I love Mt. Hood and you framed it beautifully.  From Timothy Lake?  I really like the light, the reflection and the clarity of all your details from close to far.  Would be very interested in knowing what you did to make this pop.  Congratulations!  Yes, I believe it''s Timothy Lake, I found it through GPS on my route to Mt. Hood.  This is definitely Trillium Lake, near the boat ramp. It''s not possible to get a view of Mt. Hood like this from Timothy Lake.', '2009-02-08 00:02:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5245697, 707315, 59267, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Mick:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GUTomek:</b></div><hr/><i> I love Mt. Hood and you framed it beautifully.  From Timothy Lake?  I really like the light, the reflection and the clarity of all your details from close to far.  Would be very interested in knowing what you did to make this pop.  Congratulations! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes, I believe it''s Timothy Lake, I found it through GPS on my route to Mt. Hood. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>This is definitely Trillium Lake, near the boat ramp. It''s not possible to get a view of Mt. Hood like this from Timothy Lake. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks for the correct name of the lake! I double check the web and you are right, it''s Trillium.</td>', 'Originally posted by Mick: Originally posted by william88: Originally posted by GUTomek: I love Mt. Hood and you framed it beautifully.  From Timothy Lake?  I really like the light, the reflection and the clarity of all your details from close to far.  Would be very interested in knowing what you did to make this pop.  Congratulations!  Yes, I believe it''s Timothy Lake, I found it through GPS on my route to Mt. Hood.  This is definitely Trillium Lake, near the boat ramp. It''s not possible to get a view of Mt. Hood like this from Timothy Lake.  Thanks for the correct name of the lake! I double check the web and you are right, it''s Trillium.', '2009-02-08 19:42:14.000000', NULL, 0),
